Additional attribution for the Korean common-noun vocabulary
----------------------------------------------------------

The Korean common-noun tables include a selection from the National Institute
of the Korean Language's Korean Learners' Vocabulary List (May 2003), used
under Korea Open Government License (KOGL), Type 1, with source attribution.
Source and reuse notice:
https://www.korean.go.kr/front_eng/down/down_02V.do?etc_seq=70&pageIndex=1

The selection contains 377 additional noun spellings. Historical homonym
numbers were separated, and case-particle rules and regression examples were
generated from the selected nouns. This attribution applies to the selected
data and derived tables in source and binary redistributions; the software
license above is retained. See examples/korean/lexicon/COPYING and source.json
for the selection criteria and original-file provenance. The source
organization does not endorse this project or its stemming results.
